  "question": {
    "text": "If complex number $z_{1}, z_{2}$ and 0 are vertices of equilateral triangle, then $z_{1}^{2}+z_{2}^{2}-z_{1} z_{2}$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iTZ6l",
      "text": "$0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LuRUZ",
      "text": "$z_{1}-z_{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GtyZg",
      "text": "$z_{1}+z_{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MKgrT",
      "text": "1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$z_{1}, z_{2}, 0$ are vertices of an equilateral triangle, so we have $z_{1}^{2}+z_{2}^{2}+0^{2}=z_{1} z_{2}+z_{2} \\cdot 0+0 \\cdot z_{1}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow z_{1}^{2}+z_{2}^{2}=z_{1} z_{2} \\Rightarrow z_{1}^{2}+z_{2}^{2}-z_{1} z_{2}=0\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
